From: Stoicoci Mihaita <stoicocimihaita@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: camcc-sm8250: use the active-only XO for cam_cc_xo_clk_src

cam_cc_gdsc_clk is CLK_IS_CRITICAL and sits under cam_cc_xo_clk_src, which takes
"bi_tcxo" (RPMh CXO, active+sleep vote). The critical clock keeps a sleep-set
CXO vote forever, so XO can never be shut down in s2idle. The DT already passes
"bi_tcxo_ao" (RPMH_CXO_CLK_A); newer camcc drivers (sm8450, sm8550, ...) use it
for the same always-on path.

Status: tested on q706f 14.11.2026 as a module on 7.3.4 - cameras still
enumerate, the parent becomes bi_tcxo_ao; alone it does not bring
cxsd/aosd/ddr above 0 (other blockers remain). In the series.
---
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/camcc-sm8250.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/camcc-sm8250.c
@@ -386,7 +386,7 @@
 };
 
 static const struct clk_parent_data cam_cc_parent_data_6[] = {
-	{ .fw_name = "bi_tcxo" },
+	{ .fw_name = "bi_tcxo_ao" },
 };
 
 static const struct freq_tbl ftbl_cam_cc_bps_clk_src[] = {
